### Description

Initiate an approval for creating a job plan. This API only creates an approval task and runs a full pre-check on the parameters. **No job plan is created.** Once the approval is granted, Job creates it automatically as the creator of the task.

Before calling: the target job template must exist and the caller must have the permission to view the template and create job plans in the resource scope. A job plan name must be unique within the same resource scope and job template. If the pre-check fails, an error is returned and no approval task is created.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| approval_channel | string | No | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel). The default channel configured on the server is used when omitted. Only the channel enum can be specified; the channel address and secret always come from the server configuration |
| job_template_id | long | Yes | Job template ID, must be greater than 0, and the template must already exist |
| name | string | Yes | Job plan name, 1 to 60 characters; cannot contain the HTML special characters `<`, `>`, `"`, `'`; must be unique within the same resource scope and job template |
| enable_steps | array | No | IDs of the template steps to enable in the new plan, each element being a long template step ID. All steps of the template are enabled when omitted; an empty array is not allowed; every ID must belong to the template |
| variables | array | No | Overrides for the template global variables, matched by variable name. An error is returned when the name does not exist or the type does not match the template variable; duplicated names in one request are not allowed |

##### variables[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| name | string | Yes | Global variable name in the template, matched by name (matching by variable ID is not supported); cannot be empty |
| value | string | No | Default value of the variable. Applies when the template variable type is string, namespace, ciphertext, associative array or indexed array; ignored when `follow_template` is `true`. A ciphertext variable is shown as a placeholder in the approval ticket |
| execute_target | object | No | Execution target. Provide it only when the template variable is of the execution-target list type and `follow_template` is `false`; `value` must not be provided together with it |
| follow_template | boolean | No | Whether to keep the default value defined in the template. Options: `true` (keep the template default), `false` (use `value` or `execute_target` from this request, the default). `execute_target` must not be provided when it is `true` |

##### execute_target

